title: where to find them documented
pid: 413c50fc-abc8-4be3-94a5-368516c5e370
body: |2-
  Yes—these rules are user-facing documented in docs/COMMANDS.org:51.

    The most complete parts are:

    - Text matching, options, literals, Tantivy syntax, and regex semantics (docs/COMMANDS.org:66)
    - Ranking formula and graph-role multipliers (docs/COMMANDS.org:183): BM25 × text-term coverage × context-origin multiplier.
    - The graph roles are explicitly listed: Root 100×, CycleMember ~32×, Dest 10×, HadID 10×, MultiContained ~3.2×; everything else 1×. It also says these only rerank—every match is returned.

    The Neovim-facing equivalent is docs/COMMANDS-nvim.org:63. The API-level synopsis is docs/api-and-formats.org.

    For implementation authority, see server/context.rs:1 (how graph-origin types are assigned) and server/serve/handlers/text_search.rs:448 (the combined ranking calculation).
